  "section_notes": "Final S1 imposes strict reporting (24h all incidents, 3-day customer notice). S2 sets a 10% failure limit with only pass/fail status to customers, avoiding a 5% ban on Northwind's Hearth 10 but violating Halcyon's HC-1. S3 requires new-unit shut-off in 24 months and installed-unit retrofit in 72 months; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 makes the 8/100k threshold trigger regulator review rather than mandatory recall, favouring Halcyon. Neither company signed the final version."
